parameters.text:
=A member's 7-day trial just ended and they have NOT purchased a membership.

Member: {{ $json.name }}
Trial period: {{ $json.trial_start_date }} to {{ $json.trial_end_date }}

Write a warm, persuasive but not pushy email encouraging them to convert to a membership. Include a time-limited incentive (e.g. 10% off first month, or a free PT session) to create urgency. Keep it friendly and personal, 120-150 words.

Respond ONLY with the email body text, no subject line.

=A gym member hasn't checked in for 14 days.

Member: {{ $json.name }}
Membership type: {{ $json.membership_type }}
Last check-in: {{ $json.last_checkin_date }}

Write a short, caring (not guilt-tripping) email checking in on them, asking if everything is okay, and gently encouraging them to come back. Mention that their trainer/the gym team is there to help if life got busy or motivation dipped. Keep it warm and human, 100-130 words.

Respond ONLY with the email body text, no subject line.

=It's a gym member's birthday today!

Member: {{ $json.name }}
Membership type: {{ $json.membership_type }}

Write a short, joyful, celebratory birthday email from the gym. Keep it light, fun, and genuine - not generic corporate birthday spam. Maybe include a small birthday treat idea (e.g. a free smoothie, a free guest pass for a friend). 80-100 words.

Respond ONLY with the email body text, no subject line.

=A new member just joined the gym and needs an onboarding sequence kicked off.

Member: {{ $json.name }}
Membership: {{ $json.membership_type }}
Goals: {{ $json.goals }}

Write a warm welcome email that: briefly welcomes them, mentions their stated goals to show it's personalized, gives 2-3 quick first-week tips, and invites them to book an orientation session with a trainer. 130-160 words.

Respond ONLY with the email body text, no subject line.

=A member's gym membership is expiring soon and needs a renewal follow-up.

Member: {{ $json.name }}
Membership type: {{ $json.membership_type }}
Expiry date: {{ $json.expiry_date }}

Write a friendly renewal reminder email. Mention the expiry date clearly, highlight the value they've gotten (keep it general/positive), and make renewing feel easy with a clear next step. Optionally mention a small loyalty incentive for renewing early. 110-140 words.

Respond ONLY with the email body text, no subject line.

=A new lead just came in and needs immediate contact.

Lead: {{ $json.name }}
Source: {{ $json.source }}
Interest: {{ $json.interest }}

Write a quick, friendly first-contact email. Thank them for their interest, briefly address their stated interest, and invite them to book a free trial session or call. Keep it short and easy to respond to, 90-120 words.

Respond ONLY with the email body text, no subject line.
